From 58d256533df85c38643de031f5334afa62cd2656 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "xiu.yang" <xiu.yang@sophgo.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:16:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ab): add misc controlled A/B boot partitions and
 update_misc tool

[description ]:
- Kconfig (ROOTFS options): add AB_SYSTEM ("Enable ab system", runtime
  slot selection from the misc partition) and B_SYSTEM ("Enable b system",
  default/fallback slot B; without AB_SYSTEM the slot is fixed at build
  time).
- Makefile: export CONFIG_AB_SYSTEM/CONFIG_B_SYSTEM to the u-boot build;
  when partition.xml defines rootfs_b pack the same rootfs into rootfs_a
  (rootfs.spinand) and rootfs_b (rootfs_b.spinand); new "misc" target
  packs misc.spinand (one erase block, AvbABData at offset 0 generated by
  tools/common/update_misc/gen_abmisc.py, default slot from B_SYSTEM);
  build the static update_misc tool in rootfs-prepare and install it to
  /bin when AB_SYSTEM=y; make the CFG partition optional (HAS_CFG): no
  cfg image and empty /mnt/cfg when partition.xml has no CFG.
- common_functions.sh: pack_boot also packs boot_b.spinand when boot_b
  exists; add pack_misc; pack_cfg skips when there is no CFG partition.
- envsetup_soc.sh: build_all runs pack_misc.
- tools/common/image_tool/mkcvipart.py: emit BOOT_DEV/BOOT_DEV_B,
  ROOTFS_DEV/ROOTFS_DEV_B, SPL_BOOT_PART_OFFSET (boot_a),
  SPL_BOOT_B_PART_OFFSET (boot_b), AB_MISC_OFFSET/AB_MISC_SIZE (misc)
  for u-boot; legacy BOOT/ROOTFS layouts are unchanged.
- tools/common/update_misc: new Linux tool reading/writing the 32-byte
  AvbABData record in the misc partition (raw MTD, bad block skipping,
  erase+write+verify): boot_ok [N] (refill tries of the running slot,
  default command, run from S98ab_misc), dump, get_active,
  set_active a|b [N], set_tries a|b N (per slot retry count kept in
  reserved2[0/1]), reinit. Format is compatible with the y15 misc.bin.

[root   cause]:
- BF01 needs a dual system (boot_a/rootfs_a, boot_b/rootfs_b) that can
  switch slots at runtime and fall back automatically when the active
  slot cannot boot. The SDK only supported a single BOOT/ROOTFS pair
  with hard-coded partition names in the image packing and u-boot env.
- Ported from the y15 (cv1812ha) A/B implementation; the raw-MTD misc
  layout is kept so the same metadata tooling applies.

[JIRA      ID]:TBD-BF01-AB (to be provided)
[chip project]:181x
[side effects]:
- Boards without boot_b/rootfs_b/misc in partition.xml and with
  AB_SYSTEM/B_SYSTEM unset build exactly as before (HAS_ROOTFS_B,
  HAS_CFG and the misc target are only active when the labels exist).
- Verified on cv1815ja_bf01_spinand: slot A/B boot, set_active b,
  erase boot_b -> SPL falls back to A, set_tries 5 refilled by boot_ok,
  final 9-partition layout without MISC/ENV/ENV_BAK/CFG.

[Affected *.ko/*.so/*.a] :update_misc (static bin in rootfs), misc.spinand,
boot_b.spinand, rootfs_b.spinand; no .ko/.so/.a

